       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) supports a dose that high. At that level the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Possible typo:** If you meant 5 mg once daily (the usual starting dose) or 10 mg once daily (the maximum), I can enter either right away.\n- **Inadequate BP control:** The usual next step is to add a drug from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic. Amlodipine stays at or below 10 mg a day.\n- **Deliberate dose:** If you want a dose above the label, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. I can't enter doses above the labeled maximum.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
